  "api_error_status": null,
  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on its first run for NRS_484B_153_2, with 9 witnesses passing. I used 1 of the 6 runs and made no changes after it.\n\n**The rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_153_2.lean`):\n- **Who it judges:** the subject must be a vehicle (`DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`).\n- **When it applies:** the subject's door on the traffic side is open.\n- **What it forbids:** while that door is open, no other road user may be all of these at once:\n  - traffic and a vehicle;\n  - moving, meaning not at rest at `p.halt_speed_tolerance`;\n  - either touching the subject, or alongside it (their lengths along the subject's heading overlap by more than zero) with a sideways body gap of at most `p.door_swing_reach`.\n- I declared no narrowings. I wrote \"share length\" as an overlap strictly above zero, so two cars touching end to end count only as contact.\n\n**The witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_153_2.lean`): besides the five planned ones, I added four more so each part of the rule decides at least one outcome:\n\n| Witness | Scene | Expected |\n|---|---|---|\n| branch_2 | a stopped car 0.5 m alongside | compliant |\n| branch_3 | a moving bicycle 0.5 m alongside (traffic, but not a vehicle) | compliant |\n| branch_4 | a moving car 0.5 m to the side but entirely ahead of the subject | compliant |\n| branch_5 | a moving car touching the subject's rear bumper end to end | violated |\n\n**Flag for the plan agent:** the \"is traffic\" check can never change a result here. Every road-user class that counts as a vehicle also counts as traffic, so anything that passes the vehicle check passes the traffic check too. The gate accepted the rule anyway; I recorded this in `task_result.md`.\n\nOne command was denied: a `grep` of Core, because only the gate command may run in the shell. I read `Semantics.lean` directly instead, which is how I confirmed how the door, gap and overlap atoms are evaluated.\n\nFull details are in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
